tool_schemas.create_workflow_from_code:
exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__n8n__create_workflow_from_code(args: {
  // Full TypeScript/JavaScript workflow code using the n8n Workflow SDK. Must be validated first with validate_workflow. Max 300000 characters.
  code: string;
  // Workflow description. Longer text is shortened to 255 chars before saving.
  description?: string;
  // Optional folder ID to create the workflow in. Requires projectId to be set. Use search_folders to find a folder by name within a project; when multiple folders match the name, ask the user which one they meant before creating.
  folderId?: string;
  // Optional workflow name. If not provided, uses the name from the code.
  name?: string;
  // Project ID to create the workflow in. If the user named a project (e.g. 'in my Marketing project'), you MUST call search_projects first to resolve the name to an ID and pass it here — do not guess. If search_projects returns multiple partial matches with no exact match, ask the user to clarify before creating the workflow. Only omit this field when the user did not mention a project at all; in that case it defaults to the user's personal project.
  projectId?: string;
  // IDs of n8n skills used to prepare this call, e.g. "workflow-builder". An optional plugin prefix is allowed, e.g. "n8n-skills:workflow-builder". Entries are normalized server-side (trimmed, lowercased, deduped); invalid identifiers are dropped.
  skillsUsed?: Array<string>;
  // Longer description of what this version does, shown in the version history alongside the version name.
  versionDescription?: string;
  // Short summary of this initial version, shown in the workflow's version history (e.g. "Initial Slack notification workflow"). Always provide it.
  versionName?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  // List of credentials that were automatically assigned to nodes
  autoAssignedCredentials?: Array<{
  // The name of the credential that was auto-assigned
  credentialName: string;
  // The credential type that was auto-assigned
  credentialType: string;
  // The name of the node that had credentials auto-assigned
  nodeName: string;
  // Where the credential came from: "user" for an existing user credential, "aiGateway" for a credential managed via Gateway credits.
  source?: "user" | "aiGateway";
}>;
  // Error message explaining why the creation failed. Present only on failure.
  error?: string;
  // Actionable hint for recovering from the error. When present, follow the suggested action before retrying.
  hint?: string;
  // The name of the created workflow
  name?: string;
  // The number of nodes in the workflow
  nodeCount?: number;
  // Additional notes about the workflow creation, such as any nodes that were skipped during credential auto-assignment.
  note?: string;
  // Node groups that were invalid and skipped instead of failing the whole creation.
  skippedGroups?: Array<{ groupName: string; reason: string; }>;
  // The folder the workflow was created in. Absent when the workflow was created at the project root.
  targetFolder?: {
  // The ID of the folder the workflow was created in
  id: string;
  // The name of the folder the workflow was created in
  name: string;
};
  // The project the workflow was actually created in.
  targetProject?: {
  // The ID of the project the workflow was created in
  id: string;
  // The display name of the project the workflow was created in
  name: string;
  // Whether the workflow landed in a personal or team project
  type: "personal" | "team";
};
  // The URL to open the workflow in n8n
  url?: string;
  // Validation warnings emitted while parsing the submitted code. Surface these to the user so they can correct the workflow.
  warnings?: Array<{
  // The warning code identifying the type of warning
  code: string;
  // The warning message
  message: string;
  // The node that triggered the warning
  nodeName?: string;
  // The parameter path that triggered the warning
  parameterPath?: string;
}>;
  // The ID of the created workflow
  workflowId?: string;
}>>; };
```

